<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>

Your archetype is the path you choose at character creation: it decides
which skills and spell schools you can train, gives you a starter kit of
gear, and is permanent for that character.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>
  Show your archetype (or that you haven't chosen one yet), and the full
  list with what each one offers.

  <ansi fg="command">archetype choose [name]</ansi>
  Preview an archetype: its description and starter kit.

  <ansi fg="command">archetype choose [name] confirm</ansi>
  Commit to it. This cannot be undone.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What an archetype claims</ansi>

Some skills and some spell schools belong to specific archetypes; only a
character of a claiming archetype can train that skill or learn spells of
that school. A skill or school no archetype claims is open to everyone.
Once you choose, you keep any skill or spell you already knew - choosing
never takes anything away, only opens doors closed to other archetypes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Companions</ansi>

Companions have archetypes too. Most arrive with one already; a
companion without one can be given one, once, with
<ansi fg="command">company archetype [member] [archetype]</ansi> (see
<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). A companion's archetype decides which
expedition skills they use for the company as they level up
(<ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>), and their spells and role in a battle:
a cleric heals, a wizard casts (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>), and a warrior
tackles, a rogue strikes an opening, a ranger aims a shot (<ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>).

Wizards start with Magic Missile and clerics with Minor Heal, the spells
they cast in battle.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help autoskill</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trap</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help skills</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help spells</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help train</ansi>.